{18}{My son?  Randver?  He would dare permit such an affront?  I've come here to writhe upon the blade of my sorrow, to live the thousand deaths by the ancient right of Kings.  These laws are passed down through the mountain, from the beginning of remembered time.  Your life is forfeit to them, as is my own.  Do you understand? [He raises the axe in his hand...]}{My son?  Randver?  He would dare permit such an affront?  I've come here to writhe upon the blade of my sorrow, to live the thousand deaths by the ancient right of Kings.  These laws are passed down through the mountain, from the beginning of remembered time.  Your life is forfeit to them, as is my own.  Do you understand? [He raises the axe in his hand...]}{}{4}{}{}
