{83}{Fine.  I've a story to tell...[Tell him what you know.]}{}{5}{ra -2, ra -3}{97}{}
{84}{You're words are laughable, even for a rubber-spined King.}{}{5}{}{}{co, fl 58}
{86}{[Loghaire is silent for a long time.] Forgive my harsh words before, dwarf brother.  I mean you no harm.  My crimes are heinous enough without adding to them more dwarven blood...}{[Loghaire is silent for a long time.] Forgive my harsh words before, dwarf brother.  I mean you no harm.  My crimes are heinous enough without adding to them more dwarven blood...}{}{16}{}{}
{87}{I understand, my King.  I need to know exactly what happened. }{}{5}{}{100}{}
{89}{[Loghaire is silent for a long time.] Forgive me, my elven friend.  So much has happened to me...I've raged in these caverns for so long...I know you had nothing to do with what has gone before...}{[Loghaire is silent for a long time.] Forgive me, my elven friend.  So much has happened to me...I've raged in these caverns for so long...I know you had nothing to do with what has gone before...}{}{17}{}{}
{90}{I understand, Loghaire.  But what did happen, so long ago?}{}{5}{}{100}{}
{97}{[Loghaire is silent for a long time.]  I've no words, no words.  My crime, it seems, is even more heinous than I thought.  I deserve much worse than this mere isolation..}{[Loghaire is silent for a long time.]  I've no words, no words.  My crime, it seems, is even more heinous than I thought.  I deserve much worse than this mere isolation..}{}{18}{}{}
{98}{Loghaire...I need to know exactly what happened. }{}{5}{}{100}{}
{100}{In all the time since the judgment was passed, I have never spoken of it.  My shame has held my tongue.  It seems that very shame shall now, finally, bring the betrayal to light...}{In all the time since the judgment was passed, I have never spoken of it.  My shame has held my tongue.  It seems that very shame shall now, finally, bring the betrayal to light...}{}{19}{}{}
{101}{Please...these elves who approached you...who were they?}{}{5}{}{103}{}
{103}{[Sigh.]  A delegation of elves, sent from the Silver Lady herself.  They came not long after Bates had built his first steam engine.  Technology, in the hands of the human had spread and advanced at an alarming rate.  And the elves were hit first, and hardest...}{[Sigh.]  A delegation of elves, sent from the Silver Lady herself.  They came not long after Bates had built his first steam engine.  Technology, in the hands of the human had spread and advanced at an alarming rate.  And the elves were hit first, and hardest...}{}{20}{}{}
{104}{How?  What had the spread of technology done to the elves?}{}{5}{lf1 0}{108}{lf1 1}
{105}{Why did technology spread so fast among the humans?}{}{5}{lf2 0}{116}{lf2 1}
{106}{Who is the Silver Lady?}{}{5}{lf3 0}{130}{lf3 1}
{108}{Their forests...their forests were being cleared with the help of technology--massive steam-powered clear-cutters.  The oldest groves, towering and untouched for thousands of years, were being destroyed without prejudice.  I saw much of this with my own eyes...the ancient forest of Morbihan is little more than a graveyard now...}{Their forests...their forests were being cleared with the help of technology--massive steam-powered clear-cutters.  The oldest groves, towering and untouched for thousands of years, were being destroyed without prejudice.  I saw much of this with my own eyes...the ancient forest of Morbihan is little more than a graveyard now...}{}{21}{}{ru 2046}
{109}{Why did technology spread so fast among the humans?}{}{5}{lf2 0}{116}{lf2 1}
{110}{You mentioned the Silver Lady...who is she?}{}{5}{lf3 0}{130}{lf3 1}
{111}{Were there elves living in the forests of Morbihan?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf5 0}{160}{lf5 1}
{116}{There are many reasons.  Humans, in comparison with the other races, live such short lives.  Because of this, I believe that every human action is motivated through fear...the fear of death.  You would think that this was a relative issue...that humans would learn to live with this limitation and accept it.  This is not true...}{There are many reasons.  Humans, in comparison with the other races, live such short lives.  Because of this, I believe that every human action is motivated through fear...the fear of death.  You would think that this was a relative issue...that humans would learn to live with this limitation and accept it.  This is not true...}{}{22}{}{}
{117}{And...?}{}{5}{}{119}{}
{119}{And, therefore, humans, when confronted with any situation, see it through the veil of their own mortality.  Achieve, advance, perform...humans are constantly driven by the shadow of their own death.  This fear, unfortunately, clouds their judgment, deadens their sense of right and wrong.  Humans act first, think later, and feel last of all...}{And, therefore, humans, when confronted with any situation, see it through the veil of their own mortality.  Achieve, advance, perform...humans are constantly driven by the shadow of their own death.  This fear, unfortunately, clouds their judgment, deadens their sense of right and wrong.  Humans act first, think later, and feel last of all...}{}{23}{}{}
{120}{And in terms of technology?}{}{5}{}{122}{}
{122}{When Bates was given a look at our technology, he was overcome.  As a human, his first thought was "what can I use this for?", when it should have been "what is the cost of its use?"  Technology exploded in their hands because they are NOT burdened with our longevity...humans rarely live long enough to see the consequences of their mistakes. }{When Bates was given a look at our technology, he was overcome.  As a human, his first thought was "what can I use this for?", when it should have been "what is the cost of its use?"  Technology exploded in their hands because they are NOT burdened with our longevity...humans rarely live long enough to see the consequences of their mistakes. }{}{24}{}{}
{123}{You mentioned the Silver Lady...who is she?}{}{5}{lf3 0}{130}{lf3 1}
{124}{Were there elves living in the forests of Morbihan?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf5 0}{160}{}
{125}{Have you ever spoken to the Silver Lady directly?}{}{5}{lf4 0, lf3 1}{145}{lf4 1}
{126}{What are the major differences between dwarves and elves?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf2 1, lf3 1, lf4 1, lf6 1}{181}{lf5 1}
{127}{And the Silver Lady was angry about the forests of Morbihan?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf3 1}{137}{lf5 1}
{128}{What had the spread of technology done to the elves?}{}{5}{lf1 0}{108}{lf1 1}
{130}{The Silver Lady is mother-Queen to the elves.  She is very old...much older than I, and very powerful in the ways of magick. }{The Silver Lady is mother-Queen to the elves.  She is very old...much older than I, and very powerful in the ways of magick. }{}{25}{}{}
{131}{And she was angered by what had happened to the forests...?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf3 1}{137}{}
{132}{Have you ever spoken to her directly?}{}{5}{lf4 0, lf3 1}{145}{lf4 1}
{133}{Where does she live?}{}{5}{lf6 0, lf3 1}{152}{lf6 1}
{134}{Why did technology spread so fast among the humans?}{}{5}{lf2 0}{116}{lf2 1}
{135}{What had the spread of technology done to the elves?}{}{5}{lf1 0}{108}{lf1 1}
{137}{The delegation told me that she was extremely hurt and angry about the damage that had been done...according to them, because of her age and power, she was hurt the most by the clearing...her connection to the forests was strongest of all...}{The delegation told me that she was extremely hurt and angry about the damage that had been done...according to them, because of her age and power, she was hurt the most by the clearing...her connection to the forests was strongest of all...}{}{26}{}{}
{138}{Have you ever spoken to her directly?}{}{5}{lf4 0}{145}{lf4 1}
{139}{Where does the Silver Lady live?}{}{5}{lf6 0, lf3 1}{152}{lf6 1}
{140}{Why did technology spread so fast among the humans?}{}{5}{lf2 0}{116}{lf2 1}
{141}{Were there elves living in the forests of Morbihan?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf5 0}{160}{lf5 1}
{142}{What are the major differences between dwarves and elves?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf2 1, lf3 1, lf4 1, lf6 1}{181}{lf5 1}
{143}{What had the spread of technology done to the elves?}{}{5}{lf1 0}{108}{lf1 1}
{145}{No...I'm not sure if any but elven eyes have ever been laid upon her.  Over the years, we have corresponded through messengers.  Elves and dwarves are very different, and we tend to stay away from one another.  But our relationship, as culturally strained as it may be, has always been civil.  We don't necessarily understand one another, but we've always respected the differences...}{No...I'm not sure if any but elven eyes have ever been laid upon her.  Over the years, we have corresponded through messengers.  Elves and dwarves are very different, and we tend to stay away from one another.  But our relationship, as culturally strained as it may be, has always been civil.  We don't necessarily understand one another, but we've always respected the differences...}{}{27}{}{}
{146}{Where does she live?}{}{5}{lf6 0, lf3 1}{152}{lf6 1}
{147}{About technology...why did it spread so fast among the humans?}{}{5}{lf2 0}{116}{lf2 1}
{148}{What are the major differences between dwarves and elves?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf2 1, lf3 1, lf4 1, lf6 1}{181}{}
{149}{What had the spread of technology done to the elves?}{}{5}{lf1 0}{108}{lf1 1}
{152}{In Qintarra...the oldest city of the elves, somewhere within the Glimmering Forest...}{In Qintarra...the oldest city of the elves, somewhere within the Glimmering Forest...}{}{28}{}{}
{153}{What are the major differences between dwarves and elves?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf2 1, lf3 1, lf4 1, lf6 1}{181}{}
{154}{Have you ever spoken to the Silver Lady directly?}{}{5}{lf4 0, lf3 1}{145}{lf4 1}
{155}{Why did technology spread so fast among the humans?}{}{5}{lf2 0}{116}{lf2 1}
{156}{Were there elves living in the forests of Morbihan?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf5 0}{160}{lf5 1}
{157}{And she was angered by what had happened to the forests...?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf3 1}{137}{}
{158}{What had the spread of technology done to the elves?}{}{5}{lf1 0}{108}{lf1 1}
{160}{I'm unsure, but I don't believe so...but, the delegation said that the crimes were against ALL elves.  You see,  elves feel a very strong connection to the world, to nature, and especially to forests.  It's said that elven souls reside in the oldest trees...I don't know if this is true, but I do know there to be a strong connection between living things and magick...}{I'm unsure, but I don't believe so...but, the delegation said that the crimes were against ALL elves.  You see,  elves feel a very strong connection to the world, to nature, and especially to forests.  It's said that elven souls reside in the oldest trees...I don't know if this is true, but I do know there to be a strong connection between living things and magick...}{}{29}{}{}
{161}{Why did technology spread so fast among the humans?}{}{5}{lf2 0}{116}{lf2 1}
{162}{You mentioned the Silver Lady...who is she?}{}{5}{lf3 0}{130}{lf3 1}
{163}{Have you ever spoken to the Silver Lady directly?}{}{5}{lf4 0, lf3 1}{145}{lf4 1}
{164}{What are the major differences between dwarves and elves?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf2 1, lf3 1, lf4 1, lf6 1}{181}{}
{165}{Was the Silver Lady angry about the Morbihan Forests?}{}{5}{lf1 1, lf3 1}{137}{}
{166}{What had the spread of technology done to the elves?}{}{5}{lf1 0}{108}{lf1 1}
{181}{I've said before that there is a strong connection between living things and magick, and the magick flows the most strongly in the veins of elves.  Dwarves are very different...we feel a strong connection to the earth, but in another way...we love those things which are eternal, unchangeable. Earth, Stone, Metal.  In those things are strength, but not life as you know it...}{I've said before that there is a strong connection between living things and magick, and the magick flows the most strongly in the veins of elves.  Dwarves are very different...we feel a strong connection to the earth, but in another way...we love those things which are eternal, unchangeable. Earth, Stone, Metal.  In those things are strength, but not life as you know it...}{}{30}{}{}
{182}{And the elven delegation?  What did they demand of you?}{}{5}{}{184}{}
{184}{They said that if the Black Mountain clan was not punished, there would be war.  War!  I told them that a punishment was already being decided upon, and that we, as dwarves, would deal with them.  They refused...they claimed rights as the afflicted, and therefore as the judges.  They agreed that exile was a suitable punishment...but they wanted to be the vessel of that retribution...}{They said that if the Black Mountain clan was not punished, there would be war.  War!  I told them that a punishment was already being decided upon, and that we, as dwarves, would deal with them.  They refused...they claimed rights as the afflicted, and therefore as the judges.  They agreed that exile was a suitable punishment...but they wanted to be the vessel of that retribution...}{}{31}{}{}
{185}{Are the elves a warlike people?  Is it in their nature?}{}{5}{ra -3}{189}{}
{186}{We elves are not a warlike people...it is not in our nature...}{}{5}{ra 3}{189}{}
{189}{No...I know that there was a time of violence, many years ago, among the elves...but from what I know of them, they are a very rational, peace-loving people.  They know that, ultimately, war benefits no one.  I was very surprised when they came and threatened it...}{No...I know that there was a time of violence, many years ago, among the elves...but from what I know of them, they are a very rational, peace-loving people.  They know that, ultimately, war benefits no one.  I was very surprised when they came and threatened it...}{}{32}{}{}
{190}{I see.  There seem to be some inconsistencies here...}{}{5}{}{192}{ru 2047}
{192}{Yes...the more we talk about it, I begin to get the same feeling. Yes, the elves would have been angry, but would they really have threatened war?  Morbihan was a tragedy, but directly affected none of the elven communities.  Perhaps my fear blinded me to such things before.  And now this mystery!...where are the dwarves of the Black Mountain Clan? }{Yes...the more we talk about it, I begin to get the same feeling. Yes, the elves would have been angry, but would they really have threatened war?  Morbihan was a tragedy, but directly affected none of the elven communities.  Perhaps my fear blinded me to such things before.  And now this mystery!...where are the dwarves of the Black Mountain Clan? }{}{33}{}{}
{193}{What was it you feared, Loghaire?  Why agree to the terms?}{}{5}{}{208}{}
{208}{I am very old, stranger.  You may know nothing of me, but believe me when I tell you that I've seen enough dwarven spilled to fill a thousand lifetimes.  Have you any idea what it would mean for there to be a war between the elves and the dwarves?  Arcanum it itself would not survive the conflict.  And I was so very tired of filling tombs with the bodies of my people...}{I am very old, stranger.  You may know nothing of me, but believe me when I tell you that I've seen enough dwarven spilled to fill a thousand lifetimes.  Have you any idea what it would mean for there to be a war between the elves and the dwarves?  Arcanum it itself would not survive the conflict.  And I was so very tired of filling tombs with the bodies of my people...}{}{34}{}{ru 2048}
{209}{But...}{}{5}{}{211}{}
{211}{But nothing!  I chose to spare the dwarves...the world!...the price of such a war.  What was one clan's honor in comparison with the sheer cataclysm that would result otherwise?  You ask what right they had?  None.  They merely forced a choice...and I chose the path of least resistance, the least pain.  That was my betrayal, stranger.}{But nothing!  I chose to spare the dwarves...the world!...the price of such a war.  What was one clan's honor in comparison with the sheer cataclysm that would result otherwise?  You ask what right they had?  None.  They merely forced a choice...and I chose the path of least resistance, the least pain.  That was my betrayal, stranger.}{}{35}{}{}
{212}{What do you mean?  You were merely acting out of concern...}{}{5}{}{214}{}
{214}{But that is the point!  I am King of the Dwarves!  It is my responsibility to lead them, to protect them...but, most importantly, it's my responsibility to defend their honor, their dwarven honor.  By allowing my own fear or concern, regardless of how justified that fear might be, to overshadow their honor was an unforgivable transgression...}{But that is the point!  I am King of the Dwarves!  It is my responsibility to lead them, to protect them...but, most importantly, it's my responsibility to defend their honor, their dwarven honor.  By allowing my own fear or concern, regardless of how justified that fear might be, to overshadow their honor was an unforgivable transgression...}{}{36}{}{}
{215}{Being a King isn't always easy...}{}{5}{}{218}{}
{216}{You're right...you acted both rashly and irresponsibly...}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{218}{Even as King, the choice is NEVER mine as to whether even ONE dwarf is stripped of his honor.  I should have brought this to the people, or just flatly refused from the beginning...I was a coward, a failure...and this exile is my punishment.  Given the choice now, I would have waged war against ALL of Arcanum to uphold the honor of that foolish little clan...}{Even as King, the choice is NEVER mine as to whether even ONE dwarf is stripped of his honor.  I should have brought this to the people, or just flatly refused from the beginning...I was a coward, a failure...and this exile is my punishment.  Given the choice now, I would have waged war against ALL of Arcanum to uphold the honor of that foolish little clan...}{}{37}{}{}
{219}{Yes, Loghaire.  But we can still make this right...find the truth...}{}{5}{}{223}{}
{220}{I know, I know.  That's because your Stone is still true...}{}{5}{gf1051 1}{233}{}
{221}{It's too late for that.  I just need to know who those elves were...}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{223}{I don't know, stranger.  I think that it is too late for me. }{I don't know, stranger.  I think that it is too late for me. }{}{38}{}{}
{224}{No, Loghaire.  You still have a chance to right this wrong...}{}{5}{}{228}{}
{225}{No...your Stone tells you differently...listen to it...}{}{5}{gf1051 1}{233}{}
{226}{Fine.  Your crime is unforgivable.  But at least help ME...}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{228}{No, my friend.  It is no longer my burden.  I've taken up another.  I've failed the dwarves once...I shall never do so again.  Leave me here...tell Randver he won't be seeing me anymore.  I see now that the price for my cowardice is even more costly than I'd imagined...my poor dwarven brothers...I'm so very, very sorry...}{No, my friend.  It is no longer my burden.  I've taken up another.  I've failed the dwarves once...I shall never do so again.  Leave me here...tell Randver he won't be seeing me anymore.  I see now that the price for my cowardice is even more costly than I'd imagined...my poor dwarven brothers...I'm so very, very sorry...}{}{39}{}{}
{229}{Please...}{}{5}{}{301}{}
{233}{What?  What do you know of the nature of dwarven Stone?  You, an outsider?  How could you possibly know of such things?}{What?  What do you know of the nature of dwarven Stone?  You, an outsider?  How could you possibly know of such things?}{}{40}{}{}
{234}{Randver put his faith in me...perhaps you could as well...}{}{5}{ra -2}{240}{}
{235}{Randver put his faith in me...perhaps you could as well...}{}{5}{ra 2}{237}{}
{237}{Perhaps...you are a dwarf.  Nonetheless, these are beliefs and concepts it takes a lifetime to reconcile.  How could you possibly begin to understand how I feel?}{Perhaps...you are a dwarf.  Nonetheless, these are beliefs and concepts it takes a lifetime to reconcile.  How could you possibly begin to understand how I feel?}{}{41}{}{}
{238}{I know that it is difficult to live true to both Stone and Shape...}{}{5}{}{243}{}
{240}{Perhaps...but you are not even a dwarf!   These are beliefs and concepts it takes a lifetime to reconcile.  How could you possibly begin to understand how I feel?}{Perhaps...but you are not even a dwarf!   These are beliefs and concepts it takes a lifetime to reconcile.  How could you possibly begin to understand how I feel?}{}{42}{}{}
{241}{I know that it is difficult to live by both Stone and Shape...}{}{5}{}{243}{}
{243}{Yes...I know...I've thought long and hard about this.  Dwarven Stone tells me that ANY transgression against our honor is unthinkable.  But my Shape...as King, as their father...told me to protect them.  I'd shouldered so much of their pain.  I could do it no longer...}{Yes...I know...I've thought long and hard about this.  Dwarven Stone tells me that ANY transgression against our honor is unthinkable.  But my Shape...as King, as their father...told me to protect them.  I'd shouldered so much of their pain.  I could do it no longer...}{}{43}{}{}
{244}{But, isn't part of life defining that Shape?  Learning from mistakes?}{}{5}{}{248}{}
{245}{You HAVE betrayed your people.  But you can at least help me...}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{246}{What do you see as the nature of that betrayal?}{}{5}{}{258}{}
{248}{Yes.  Your words sound true, stranger.  I know that no man is flawless.  BUT, I also know that each man's load to bear is different.  A larger load carries more responsibility.  Mine is heaviest of all...therefore the price for my betrayal must be the most costly...}{Yes.  Your words sound true, stranger.  I know that no man is flawless.  BUT, I also know that each man's load to bear is different.  A larger load carries more responsibility.  Mine is heaviest of all...therefore the price for my betrayal must be the most costly...}{}{44}{}{}
{249}{You'll continue to pay it...at least tell me what I need to know...}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{250}{What is the nature of that betrayal?}{}{5}{}{258}{}
{251}{This isolation is nothing...you've yet to pay the worst of it...}{}{5}{}{253}{}
{253}{What?  What do you mean?}{What?  What do you mean?}{}{45}{}{}
{254}{You've been a coward before...you're acting no different now.}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{255}{It is much more costly to FACE your mistakes, and right them.}{}{5}{}{267}{}
{258}{The nature of the betrayal?  I've failed my people...isn't that what is most important here?  The betrayal was against their Stone...it seems, sadly, that my own Stone is flawed...}{The nature of the betrayal?  I've failed my people...isn't that what is most important here?  The betrayal was against their Stone...it seems, sadly, that my own Stone is flawed...}{}{46}{}{}
{259}{No...that was Lorek's flaw.  Yours is a conflict of Shape...}{}{5}{gf1063 1}{263}{}
{260}{The failure is not one of Stone, but of Shape...don't you see?}{}{5}{gf1063 0}{263}{}
{261}{Your failure is not in question.  What are you going to do about it?}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{263}{You shame me, stranger.  Your words are harsh...but undeniably true.  Perhaps you are correct...but it doesn't change what I've done, nor the price I need to pay.  It is best if you just leave an old dwarf here to rot...it is your place to right this wrong...}{You shame me, stranger.  Your words are harsh...but undeniably true.  Perhaps you are correct...but it doesn't change what I've done, nor the price I need to pay.  It is best if you just leave an old dwarf here to rot...it is your place to right this wrong...}{}{47}{}{}
{264}{No.  YOU must pay the price.  I cannot do this for you.}{}{5}{}{267}{}
{265}{I'll have no trouble doing that.  But I need your help, first...}{}{5}{}{298}{}
{267}{How, then?  How can I do so?}{How, then?  How can I do so?}{}{48}{}{}
{268}{You must return to your people.  Be true to Stone AND Shape...}{}{5}{}{270}{}
{270}{By Alberich!  You are right!  I've been blinded by my own shame...and not seen the true betrayal.  I've betrayed myself, and my people along with me.  I shall return, stranger!  I shall be King!  By the name of Thunder Stone, I swear it!}{By Alberich!  You are right!  I've been blinded by my own shame...and not seen the true betrayal.  I've betrayed myself, and my people along with me.  I shall return, stranger!  I shall be King!  By the name of Thunder Stone, I swear it!}{}{49}{}{gf1050 1, ru 2049, xp 5, rp 1054, fp}
{271}{I'm so very glad.  But I still need some information...}{}{5}{}{273}{}
{273}{Of course...I'll do anything within my power to help you...}{Of course...I'll do anything within my power to help you...}{}{50}{}{}
{274}{These elves who came to you...how can I find them?}{}{5}{}{276}{}
{276}{As I said, they were supposedly sent from the Silver Lady.  I know very little of them.  But I do have a name...perhaps that will be enough for you to uncover this mystery...}{As I said, they were supposedly sent from the Silver Lady.  I know very little of them.  But I do have a name...perhaps that will be enough for you to uncover this mystery...}{}{51}{}{}
{277}{What is that name?}{}{5}{}{279}{}
{279}{The delegation was sent by someone named M'in Gorad, and I had many correspondences with this elf.  Here is a letter that was sent to me by him...[He hands you a letter.]}{The delegation was sent by someone named M'in Gorad, and I had many correspondences with this elf.  Here is a letter that was sent to me by him...[He hands you a letter.]}{}{52}{}{qu1017 4, in -5203}
{280}{Where can I find this M'in Gorad?}{}{5}{}{282}{}
{282}{I'm unsure.  The entire situation reeks of deception.  I would tell you to seek him in Qintarra, but I don't even know if the delegation was sent from there or not.  Regardless, you may want to begin your search there...the Silver Lady might know of this M'in Gorad.}{I'm unsure.  The entire situation reeks of deception.  I would tell you to seek him in Qintarra, but I don't even know if the delegation was sent from there or not.  Regardless, you may want to begin your search there...the Silver Lady might know of this M'in Gorad.}{}{53}{}{ss 8, qu1018 2}
{283}{And where is Qintarra?}{}{5}{}{285}{}
{285}{I don't know, unfortunately.  The location of Qintarra is a well-guarded secret.  But I do know it lies within the Glimmering forests.  The small town of Stillwater lies near the edge of that forest.  Perhaps there you might find someone who knows where it is...here, I'll mark your map with Stillwater's location...}{I don't know, unfortunately.  The location of Qintarra is a well-guarded secret.  But I do know it lies within the Glimmering forests.  The small town of Stillwater lies near the edge of that forest.  Perhaps there you might find someone who knows where it is...here, I'll mark your map with Stillwater's location...}{}{54}{}{mm 10}
{286}{Thank you, Loghaire.  I will do my best to find out the truth...}{}{5}{}{288}{}
{288}{Wait!  I'm much to blame for this situation...my fear and cowardice have helped in bringing about this tragedy.  I feel I must do something to help you.  Please, take Harrow, the first-axe of my family.  Its blade strikes true and deep in the hands of the righteous, especially if those hands are dwarven.  Within it is the strength of the Thunder Stones...I give it to you...}{Wait!  I'm much to blame for this situation...my fear and cowardice have helped in bringing about this tragedy.  I feel I must do something to help you.  Please, take Harrow, the first-axe of my family.  Its blade strikes true and deep in the hands of the righteous, especially if those hands are dwarven.  Within it is the strength of the Thunder Stones...I give it to you...}{}{55}{}{in -2004}
{289}{I will put it to good use...}{}{5}{gf1056 1}{292}{}
{290}{I will put it to good use...}{}{5}{gf1056 0}{295}{}
{292}{I'm sure you will.  Godspeed on your quest, my friend.  And...if you do find out what happened to the Black Mountain Clan, return to me.  I would be VERY interested in finding out what really happened to them.  VERY interested...}{I'm sure you will.  Godspeed on your quest, my friend.  And...if you do find out what happened to the Black Mountain Clan, return to me.  I would be VERY interested in finding out what really happened to them.  VERY interested...}{}{56}{}{ru 2050, qu1016 2}
{293}{I just might do that.  Good bye, Loghaire.}{}{5}{}{-17}{}
{295}{I'm sure you will.  Godspeed on your quest, my friend.  There is an easier way to return to the surface...there is a secret passage just behind me that Randver uses when he comes to speak with me.  Within it you will encounter no trouble.  Good luck.}{I'm sure you will.  Godspeed on your quest, my friend.  There is an easier way to return to the surface...there is a secret passage just behind me that Randver uses when he comes to speak with me.  Within it you will encounter no trouble.  Good luck.}{}{57}{}{}
{296}{Thank you, and good bye...}{}{5}{}{-17}{}
{298}{Your words bite deep, stranger.  Your story has done little to ease my shame...if anything, it serves as a reminder of my failure.  I will speak no further of this, ever.  I can give you no help but this...[he hands you a folded scrap of paper.]}{Your words bite deep, stranger.  Your story has done little to ease my shame...if anything, it serves as a reminder of my failure.  I will speak no further of this, ever.  I can give you no help but this...[he hands you a folded scrap of paper.]}{}{58}{}{}
{299}{What?  What do you mean?}{}{5}{}{301}{}
{301}{Take this...a letter, sent to me from the elven delegation.  Within it is a name, M'in Gorad.  It's all I have...and all I'm willing to give.  Perhaps you should seek out Qintarra, city of the elves.   I know not where it is, but the village of Stillwater is near the edge of the Glimmering Forest, in which, it is said, Qintarra lies.  Maybe someone there will know where to find it.  [He marks your map.]}{Take this...a letter, sent to me from the elven delegation.  Within it is a name, M'in Gorad.  It's all I have...and all I'm willing to give.  Perhaps you should seek out Qintarra, city of the elves.   I know not where it is, but the village of Stillwater is near the edge of the Glimmering Forest, in which, it is said, Qintarra lies.  Maybe someone there will know where to find it.  [He marks your map.]}{}{59}{}{mm 10, in -5203, qu1018 2, ss 8, qu1016 2, qu1017 4}
{302}{But...}{}{5}{}{}{fl 304}
{304}{I'll say no more.  Leave me...I return to my exile.  I am nothing.}{I'll say no more.  Leave me...I return to my exile.  I am nothing.}{}{60}{}{lf8 1, ru 2051}
{317}{Yes, I am Loghaire!  And you have made a TERRIBLE mistake!  This insolence is unforgivable!  The violation of my ancient right for solitude in exile is not broken so easily!  Your life hangs in the balance stranger!  Speak quickly, lest you taste the fury of Harrow...[He hefts a double-edged axe from his belt.]}{Yes, I am Loghaire!  And you have made a TERRIBLE mistake!  This insolence is unforgivable!  The violation of my ancient right for solitude in exile is not broken so easily!  Your life hangs in the balance stranger!  Speak quickly, lest you taste the fury of Harrow...[He hefts a double-edged axe from his belt.]}{}{61}{}{}
{318}{Wait!  Lissen...!}{}{-4}{}{327}{}
{319}{You funny when mad!  Spit fly out of your mouth!}{}{-4}{}{322}{lc1 1}
{320}{Ooops!  I go now...}{}{-4}{}{335}{}
{322}{YOU HAVE THE AUDACITY TO TAKE THAT TONE WITH ME?  I'VE SPILLED OCEANS OF BLOOD WITH THIS AXE...THE BODIES OF THE FALLEN WOULD MAKE A MOUNTAIN TO HIDE THE SUN! AND YOU DARE...?}{YOU HAVE THE AUDACITY TO TAKE THAT TONE WITH ME?  I'VE SPILLED OCEANS OF BLOOD WITH THIS AXE...THE BODIES OF THE FALLEN WOULD MAKE A MOUNTAIN TO HIDE THE SUN! AND YOU DARE...?}{}{62}{}{}
{323}{No!  Just joking!  Please, Lissen!}{}{-4}{}{327}{}
{324}{Ha!  You even funnier looking than before!}{}{-4}{}{}{co, fl 333}
{327}{NO!  YOU LISTEN!  I've come here to writhe upon the blade of my sorrow, to live the thousand deaths by the ancient right of Kings.  These laws are passed down through the mountain, from the beginning of remembered time.  Your life is forfeit to them, as is my own.  Do you understand? [He raises the axe in his hand...]}{NO!  YOU LISTEN!  I've come here to writhe upon the blade of my sorrow, to live the thousand deaths by the ancient right of Kings.  These laws are passed down through the mountain, from the beginning of remembered time.  Your life is forfeit to them, as is my own.  Do you understand? [He raises the axe in his hand...]}{}{63}{}{}
{328}{N-n-noo...I no unnerstand.  Just need talk!  Please!}{}{-4}{}{342}{}
{329}{Ha!  HA!  You make dumb faces! }{}{-4}{lc1 0}{322}{lc1 1}
{330}{Ha!  HA!  You make dumb faces! }{}{-4}{lc1 1}{}{co, fl 333}
{331}{Me scared.  Me leave.}{}{-4}{}{335}{}
{333}{Those words will be your last, fool.  Harrow, my family's axe, will now be your judge...}{Those words will be your last, fool.  Harrow, my family's axe, will now be your judge...}{}{64}{}{}
{335}{No!  I'm very sorry, but you've made a terrible, terrible mistake.  You're going nowhere...I've come here to writhe upon the blade of my sorrow, to live the thousand deaths by the ancient right of Kings, and you presume to disturb me?  These laws are passed down from the beginning of remembered time, and your life is forfeit to them. Do you understand? [He raises the axe in his hand...] }{No!  I'm very sorry, but you've made a terrible, terrible mistake.  You're going nowhere...I've come here to writhe upon the blade of my sorrow, to live the thousand deaths by the ancient right of Kings, and you presume to disturb me?  These laws are passed down from the beginning of remembered time, and your life is forfeit to them. Do you understand? [He raises the axe in his hand...] }{}{65}{}{}
{336}{What?  What you saying?  I dumb!  Please, no!}{}{-4}{}{342}{}
{337}{Stupid Logare.  You make me mad!  I kill you now!}{}{-4}{}{}{co, fl 333}
{342}{What?  What is wrong with you, stranger?  Are you dim?  [The axe lowers slightly.]  What is a simpleton like you doing roaming the caverns of the Dredge?}{What?  What is wrong with you, stranger?  Are you dim?  [The axe lowers slightly.]  What is a simpleton like you doing roaming the caverns of the Dredge?}{}{66}{}{}
{343}{Yes!  Me dumb!  But I need talk to Logare!}{}{-4}{}{345}{}
{345}{Then speak, foolish one.  I've no stomach for slaughtering idiots, but my patience runs thin.}{Then speak, foolish one.  I've no stomach for slaughtering idiots, but my patience runs thin.}{}{67}{}{}
{346}{Okey-dokey...[Tell him what you know.]}{}{-4}{}{348}{}
{348}{Oh no.  [Loghaire puts his head in his hands.]  My crime is even worse than I'd imagined.  Mere exile is no suitable punishment for the atrocity I've committed.}{Oh no.  [Loghaire puts his head in his hands.]  My crime is even worse than I'd imagined.  Mere exile is no suitable punishment for the atrocity I've committed.}{}{68}{}{}
{349}{What wrong, Logare?}{}{-4}{}{351}{}
{351}{It's no longer important, friend.  There's nothing I can do to right this wrong...}{It's no longer important, friend.  There's nothing I can do to right this wrong...}{}{69}{}{}
{352}{What happened?  Why elves send away BMC?}{}{-4}{}{354}{}
{354}{The elves?  They had threatened war.  War!  [To himself.] Do you know what a war between the elves and the dwarves would mean?  Arcanum wouldn't have survived the conflict...and yet now, knowing this about the Black Mountain Clan, I would have warred against the entire world to defend their honor...}{The elves?  They had threatened war.  War!  [To himself.] Do you know what a war between the elves and the dwarves would mean?  Arcanum wouldn't have survived the conflict...and yet now, knowing this about the Black Mountain Clan, I would have warred against the entire world to defend their honor...}{}{70}{}{ru 2048}
{355}{Why elves wanna fight?}{}{-4}{}{357}{}
{357}{Technology...technology had ruined their forests...steam-powered logging machines...and they blamed the Black Mountain Clan for sharing their technology with Bates.  [Sigh.]  It doesn't matter anymore.  It seems I've been fooled, and have sacrificed my dwarven brethren to some darker plot.  It seems I was never fit to lead...}{Technology...technology had ruined their forests...steam-powered logging machines...and they blamed the Black Mountain Clan for sharing their technology with Bates.  [Sigh.]  It doesn't matter anymore.  It seems I've been fooled, and have sacrificed my dwarven brethren to some darker plot.  It seems I was never fit to lead...}{}{71}{}{ru 2046}
{358}{Who were elves?  Where I find them?}{}{-4}{}{360}{}
{360}{Take this...a letter, sent to me from the elves who approached me.  Within it is a name, M'in Gorad.  Perhaps you should seek out Qintarra, city of the elves.   I know not where it is, but the village of Stillwater is near the edge of the Glimmering Forest, in which, it is said, Qintarra lies.  Maybe someone there will know where to find it.  [He marks your map.] This is all I have...and all I'm willing to give. }{Take this...a letter, sent to me from the elves who approached me.  Within it is a name, M'in Gorad.  Perhaps you should seek out Qintarra, city of the elves.   I know not where it is, but the village of Stillwater is near the edge of the Glimmering Forest, in which, it is said, Qintarra lies.  Maybe someone there will know where to find it.  [He marks your map.] This is all I have...and all I'm willing to give. }{}{72}{}{qu1017 4, qu1018 2, in -5203, ss 8, mm 10, ru 2051}
{361}{Uh....}{}{-4}{}{}{fl 363}
{363}{I'll say no more.  Leave me...I return to my exile.  I am nothing.}{I'll say no more.  Leave me...I return to my exile.  I am nothing.}{}{73}{}{lf9 1}
{365}{I make preparations to return to my clan!  Good luck, my friend!}{I make preparations to return to my clan!  Good luck, my friend!}{}{74}{}{}
{367}{Wh-h-hat?  What is this?  I am dead!  You've killed me, and now you call me back to the lands of the living?  And the pain I feel...worse here than anything I ever felt in life...!}{Wh-h-hat?  What is this?  I am dead!  You've killed me, and now you call me back to the lands of the living?  And the pain I feel...worse here than anything I ever felt in life...!}{}{75}{}{}
{368}{Yes, Loghaire.  And the pain will continue until you answer me...}{}{5}{}{371}{}
{369}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
{371}{What?  What...Ahhh!  The pain is great!  Perhaps only this is a true punishment for my crimes...I must endure...}{What?  What...Ahhh!  The pain is great!  Perhaps only this is a true punishment for my crimes...I must endure...}{}{76}{}{}
{372}{What are you talking about?  What crimes?}{}{5}{}{374}{}
{373}{E:}{}{5}{}{0}{}
